; Generated I5 descriptor-driven native object skeleton.
;
; The initialized caller section is the ATOM-built startup shape from
; tests/native-i5-caller.asm.  COMSTART establishes the native stack, BOOTINIT
; clears the linked BSS envelope and calls the provider's heap, collector and
; execution services before entering the generated slot.  The printer returns
; through BDOS and leaves the generated value in RESULT/RESTAG.
;
; Section 1 is a fixed 512-byte initialized image:
;   startup and printer, BOOTDESC, STORDESC, TOPDESC, RTCONFIG, and GENCODE.
; Section 2 is the variable result stream at run offset $0200. Section 3 is
; the bounded literal recipe at run offset $0300. Section 4 is the 136-byte
; zero-initialized runtime envelope at run offset $1000. Section 5 is an
; allocated executable image for the generated body; its length and image are
; patched from the lowered code before publication. The five BSS ranges reserve
; roots, activations, workspace, bitmap and heap; four more identify the
; initialized descriptors and runtime configuration.
;
; N4COM retains the old 128-byte standalone message printer.  N8EMIT uses it
; only for the current static COM compatibility path; NOBJ publication retains
; the descriptor-driven startup and service relocations below.
